{
  "id": "gitlab",
  "name": "GitLab",
  "kind": "site",
  "category": "Development",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "chrome.exe",
      "msedge.exe",
      "firefox.exe",
      "brave.exe",
      "vivaldi.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.google.Chrome",
      "com.microsoft.edgemac",
      "org.mozilla.firefox",
      "com.brave.Browser",
      "com.apple.Safari"
    ],
    "window_title": [
      "GitLab"
    ]
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://docs.gitlab.com/user/shortcuts/",
    "https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/raw/master/doc/user/shortcuts.md"
  ],
  "note": "Two-key shortcuts written as \"g\"+\"x\" style throughout the doc (Project navigation, and the \"c\"+\"r\" copy-reference shortcuts repeated in Issues/Merge requests/Incidents/Epics) are sequential presses, not held chords, per the doc's own \"g, then x\" phrasing for the equivalent Global entry; each is listed as a sequence of two single-key chords. Rows offering two interchangeable keys (\"s\" or \"/\", \"]\" or \"j\", arrow or vim-style hjkl in Repository graph) are listed as a primary action plus an \"(alternate)\" action, since the grammar has no way to express two bindings for one action. The source's \"Redo\" row in the Rich text editor's Editing table documents Cmd+Shift+V / Ctrl+Shift+V, identical to the \"Paste without formatting\" row directly above it - almost certainly a documentation typo (likely meant Cmd+Shift+Z) - but is transcribed verbatim rather than guessed, per the no-guessing rule. \"Open the Web IDE\" (.) is documented three times (Global, Project, Project files) and is listed once per context since the doc repeats it in each section's table. The current docs have no standalone \"Filtered search\" section; the closest documented shortcut is the Global \"Focus filter bar\" (f) entry. GitLab Duo Chat shortcuts are IDE-extension shortcuts (VS Code / JetBrains / Visual Studio), not shortcuts of the gitlab.com website itself, but are included because the source doc documents them on this page; IDE support is noted in each action's context. Not expressible, so left out: nothing else identified as mouse-only in this doc.",
  "actions": [
    { "name": "Show or hide the shortcut reference sheet", "context": "", "windows": { "type": "keys", "chord": "/" }, "mac": { "type": "keys", "chord": "/" } },
    { "name": "Go to the homepage", "context": "", "windows": { "type": "keys", "chord": "Shift+H" }, "mac": { "type": "keys", "chord": "Shift+H" } },
    { "name": "Go to your Projects page", "context": "", "windows": { "type": "keys", "chord": "Shift+P" }, "mac": { "type": "keys", "chord": "Shift+P" } },
    { "name": "Go to your Groups page", "context": "", "windows": { "type": "keys", "chord": "Shift+G" }, "mac": { "type": "keys", "chord": "Shift+G" } },
